              "id": "CVE-2024-47081",
              "name": "CVE-2024-47081",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-47081: Requests vulnerable to .netrc credentials leak via malicious URLs"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "### Impact\n\nDue to a URL parsing issue, Requests releases prior to 2.32.4 may leak .netrc credentials to third parties for specific maliciously-crafted URLs.\n\n### Workarounds\nFor older versions of Requests, use of the .netrc file can be disabled with `trust_env=False` on your Requests Session ([docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/#requests.Session.trust_env)).\n\n### References\nhttps://github.com/psf/requests/pull/6965\nhttps://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2",
                "markdown": "### Impact\n\nDue to a URL parsing issue, Requests releases prior to 2.32.4 may leak .netrc credentials to third parties for specific maliciously-crafted URLs.\n\n### Workarounds\nFor older versions of Requests, use of the .netrc file can be disabled with `trust_env=False` on your Requests Session ([docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/#requests.Session.trust_env)).\n\n### References\nhttps://github.com/psf/requests/pull/6965\nhttps://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2"
              },
