              ],
              "help": {
                "text": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2024-47081](https://osv.dev/list?q=CVE-2024-47081)**\n(Also published as: [PYSEC-2026-1872](https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-1872), [GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7](https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7), ).\n\n## [PYSEC-2026-1872](https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-1872)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Due to a URL parsing issue, Requests releases prior to 2.32.4 may leak .netrc credentials to third parties for specific maliciously-crafted URLs.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e For older versions of Requests, use of the .netrc file can be disabled with `trust_env=False` on your Requests Session ([docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/#requests.Session.trust_env)).\n\u003e \n\u003e ### References\n\u003e https://github.com/psf/requests/pull/6965\n\u003e https://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n## [GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7](https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Due to a URL parsing issue, Requests releases prior to 2.32.4 may leak .netrc credentials to third parties for specific maliciously-crafted URLs.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e For older versions of Requests, use of the .netrc file can be disabled with `trust_env=False` on your Requests Session ([docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/#requests.Session.trust_env)).\n\u003e \n\u003e ### References\n\u003e https://github.com/psf/requests/pull/6965\n\u003e https://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/tmp/tmp.FjLTxcKRog/repo/requirements.txt | requests | 2.19.0 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7 | requests | 2.32.4 |\n| PYSEC-2026-1872 | requests | 2.32.4 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/tmp/tmp.FjLTxcKRog/repo/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2024-47081\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n",
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2024-47081](https://osv.dev/list?q=CVE-2024-47081)**\n(Also published as: [PYSEC-2026-1872](https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-1872), [GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7](https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7), ).\n\n## [PYSEC-2026-1872](https://osv.dev/vulnerability/PYSEC-2026-1872)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Due to a URL parsing issue, Requests releases prior to 2.32.4 may leak .netrc credentials to third parties for specific maliciously-crafted URLs.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e For older versions of Requests, use of the .netrc file can be disabled with `trust_env=False` on your Requests Session ([docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/#requests.Session.trust_env)).\n\u003e \n\u003e ### References\n\u003e https://github.com/psf/requests/pull/6965\n\u003e https://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n## [GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7](https://osv.dev/vulnerability/GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e ### Impact\n\u003e \n\u003e Due to a URL parsing issue, Requests releases prior to 2.32.4 may leak .netrc credentials to third parties for specific maliciously-crafted URLs.\n\u003e \n\u003e ### Workarounds\n\u003e For older versions of Requests, use of the .netrc file can be disabled with `trust_env=False` on your Requests Session ([docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/#requests.Session.trust_env)).\n\u003e \n\u003e ### References\n\u003e https://github.com/psf/requests/pull/6965\n\u003e https://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2025/Jun/2\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/tmp/tmp.FjLTxcKRog/repo/requirements.txt | requests | 2.19.0 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-9hjg-9r4m-mvj7 | requests | 2.32.4 |\n| PYSEC-2026-1872 | requests | 2.32.4 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`osv-scanner.toml` file located in the same directory as the lockfile containing the vulnerable dependency.\n\nSee the format and more options in our documentation here: https://google.github.io/osv-scanner/configuration/\n\nAdd or append these values to the following config files to ignore this vulnerability:\n\n`/tmp/tmp.FjLTxcKRog/repo/osv-scanner.toml`\n\n```\n[[IgnoredVulns]]\nid = \"CVE-2024-47081\"\nreason = \"Your reason for ignoring this vulnerability\"\n```\n"
